        "sentence": "Connects an Arduino Uno WiFi Rev2 or an ESP32 board to Azure IoT Central: WiFi, on-device DPS provisioning, MQTT telemetry, and cloud-to-device control.",
        "paragraph": "Replaces firedog1024/arduino-uno-wifi-iotc + the archived Azure/dps-keygen tool. No PC-side tooling required -- the board provisions itself via Azure's Device Provisioning Service at boot. Includes writable-property support for controlling actuators (LEDs, buzzers) from the IoT Central dashboard, and reading another device's telemetry via the IoT Central REST API. See the 28 included examples, grouped by mode (send to cloud / control from cloud / react to another device) and ordered easiest-to-hardest within each group.",
